Package: GsheetGenie
Title: Build Analytical Google Sheets from R
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Jesse", "Brandt", , "jesse.a.brandt@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Build Google Sheets whose derived columns are live formulas
    rather than pre-computed values. Wrap a data frame with 'as_sheet_frame()'
    and a lazy 'dplyr::mutate()' records each tidy expression, translating it
    to A1 spreadsheet-formula syntax written via 'googlesheets4'. Also ships
    eager helpers for data tables flanked by live-formula summary rows
    (sums, means, etc.). Focuses on formula-and-layout logic; no formatting
    or styling.
